     "text": "This round keeps the best tile size (4096) and makes one deliberate change: ordinary vectorized global loads and stores instead of TMA. The change is not yet measured, so whether it beats 0.0218 ms is unknown.\n\n**Why this might help.** At 0.0218 ms the kernel moves about 120 MB (two 40 MB inputs and one 40 MB output). That is roughly 5.8 TB/s, against a measured peak of 6.54 TB/s. TMA routes each tile through shared memory, so every block waits for the bulk load to land before adding, then waits for the bulk store before it exits. Plain 128-bit loads go straight to registers, with many loads in flight per thread. That should cut per-block latency and leave more memory requests outstanding.\n\n**What is unchanged.** The add stays in fp16 in one launch. A partial last tile is still read with zero padding and stored with out-of-range elements dropped, so no index at or beyond `n` is written.\n\n```python title=\"impl_cutile.py\"\nimport torch\nimport cuda.tile as ct\n\nConstInt = ct.Constant[int]\n\n# Fixed configuration literals\n_TILE = 4096\n_ALLOW_TMA = False\n\n\n@ct.kernel\ndef _vector_add_kernel(x, y, out, TILE: ConstInt):\n    bid = ct.bid(0)\n    # Bounds-padded loads for a possible partial last tile.\n    # Direct (non-TMA) vectorized global loads straight into registers.\n    a = ct.load(x, (bid,), (TILE,), padding_mode=ct.PaddingMode.ZERO,\n                allow_tma=False)\n    b = ct.load(y, (bid,), (TILE,), padding_mode=ct.PaddingMode.ZERO,\n                allow_tma=False)\n    # Add in the input dtype (fp16), exactly like the reference.\n    c = a + b\n    # Bounds-clipped store: elements beyond n are dropped.\n    ct.store(out, (bid,), c, allow_tma=False)\n\n\ndef run(x, y):\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    grid = (ct.cdiv(n, _TILE),)\n    ct.launch(torch.cuda.current_stream(), grid, _vector_add_kernel,\n              (x, y, out, _TILE))\n    return out\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return {\"TILE\": 4096, \"allow_tma\": False}\n```",
     "type": "text"
    }
